:: Ember {"position":"900,25","size":"100,100"}
!! Chapter II — Ember Tonic
The page says: “POUR to the silver band. HEAT Ember Root. Nightbell Leaves — ~~~~~~~. Add Sun Honey just as it is. MIX three times. The order matters!” Which sequence will you use?

<<link "Heated Ember Root → sliced Nightbell Leaves → raw Sun Honey; mix 3" "EmberSuccess">><<set $successes += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Raw Sun Honey → heated Ember Root → sliced Nightbell Leaves; mix 3" "EmberFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Heated Ember Root → heated Nightbell Leaves → raw Sun Honey; mix 3" "EmberFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>


:: EmberFail {"position":"1025,25","size":"100,100"}
!! The Ember Turns to Smoke
A cloud of orange smoke rolls across the bench. The order or preparation is wrong. The journal preserves the result so you can correct the next attempt.

<<link "Read the notes and retry Ember Tonic" "Ember">><<set $journal += 1>><</link>>


:: EmberSuccess {"position":"1150,25","size":"100,100"}
!! The Second Page Returns
The tonic glows warm amber. A second parchment fragment emerges: “To balance flame, bind it with frost.” Only the most complex formula remains.

<<link "Turn to Frostfire Brew" "Frostfire">><</link>>


:: Ending {"position":"400,150","size":"100,100"}
!! Epilogue
The laboratory is whole again. The apprentice has restored the three recipes and learned that errors are clues, not endings. Your choices shape the closing note.

<<if $careful >= $bold>>You became a thoughtful scholar who reads every clue before acting.<<else>>You became a fearless experimenter who learns by testing possibilities.<</if>>
You made <<= $failures>> unsuccessful attempts and consulted the journal <<= $journal>> times.

<<link "Begin a new story" "Start">><<set $careful = 0>><<set $bold = 0>><<set $journal = 0>><<set $failures = 0>><<set $successes = 0>><</link>>


:: Experiment {"position":"400,25","size":"100,100"}
!! A Bold Beginning
You rush to the cauldron. A stray spark stains your sleeve. Perhaps the missing pages will be recovered through trial and error rather than caution.

<<link "Open the Moonlight Elixir page" "Moonlight">><</link>>


:: FrostFail {"position":"150,150","size":"100,100"}
!! A Frostfire Backlash
The cauldron flashes blue and orange, then falls quiet. One preparation or the stirring count is wrong. You can still try again.

<<link "Consult the journal and retry" "Frostfire">><<set $journal += 1>><</link>>


:: FrostSuccess {"position":"275,150","size":"100,100"}
!! The Final Page
The potion holds both blue frost and amber flame without breaking apart. The book’s final missing page materializes. A handwritten message appears: “The book was never meant to give every answer. It was meant to teach you to discover them.”

<<link "Read your ending" "Ending">><</link>>


:: Frostfire {"position":"25,150","size":"100,100"}
!! Chapter III — Frostfire Brew
The last recipe reads: “POUR to the silver band. Frost Lily, sliced. Dragon Scale, sliced AND heated. Glowcap Mushrooms, ~~~~~~. A drop of Star Essence to finish. MIX ~~ times.” The formula depends on every step.

<<link "Sliced Frost Lily → sliced+heated Dragon Scale → heated Glowcap → raw Star Essence; mix 4" "FrostSuccess">><<set $successes += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Sliced Frost Lily → heated Dragon Scale → raw Glowcap → raw Star Essence; mix 4" "FrostFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Correct ingredients in order, but mix twice" "FrostFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>


:: MoonFail {"position":"650,25","size":"100,100"}
!! A Silver Mishap
The cauldron sputters and the apprentice coughs. Your journal points to the first mismatch: ingredient preparation or stirring count. The recipe is still recoverable.

<<link "Review the journal and try again" "Moonlight">><<set $journal += 1>><</link>>


:: MoonSuccess {"position":"775,25","size":"100,100"}
!! The First Page Returns
Silver light fills the vial. The hidden number becomes clear: TWO. A strip of parchment reappears, carrying the message: “Fire reveals what shadow conceals.”

<<link "Turn to Ember Tonic" "Ember">><</link>>


:: Moonlight {"position":"525,25","size":"100,100"}
!! Chapter I — Moonlight Elixir
The first page reads: “POUR to the silver band. Take Moonstone, SLICE it, and send it TO THE POT. MIX ~~~ times. SERVE.” The missing number must be deduced. How will you prepare the first brew?

<<link "Slice Moonstone, pour to the silver band, mix twice" "MoonSuccess">><<set $successes += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Heat Moonstone and mix twice" "MoonFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Slice Moonstone but mix four times" "MoonFail">><<set $failures += 1>><</link>>


:: Start {"position":"150,25","size":"100,100"}
!! The Missing Pages
The laboratory is silent. Your master’s recipe book lies open, its instructions scarred by ink and torn edges. Three recipes remain: Moonlight Elixir, Ember Tonic, and Frostfire Brew. Each successful brew may restore a fragment of the lost knowledge.

<<link "Read the master’s note" "Study">><<set $careful += 1>><</link>>
<<link "Begin experimenting immediately" "Experiment">><<set $bold += 1>><</link>>


